/*
 * The theme every runtime panel in Snackdown is drawn with.
 *
 * A theme rather than a stylesheet linked from each document. Four UXML files were each carrying
 * their own <Style src="Snackdown.uss">, which works and means the fifth one added will forget,
 * and that a change to what "the UI" is styled with is a change to four files. A theme is set once
 * on the PanelSettings and reaches everything that panel draws.
 *
 * It imports two things and defines nothing of its own. The default runtime theme first, because
 * it is what gives Unity's own controls - the dropdown's list, the text field's cursor, the
 * scroller - any appearance at all; dropping it does not give a blank slate, it gives unstyled
 * internals. Then Snackdown.uss, which is where every rule this project wrote actually lives.
 *
 * The order matters and is the usual one: the general theme, then the specific overrides.
 */

@import url("unity-theme://default");
@import url("project://database/Assets/_Project/UI/Snackdown.uss");
